{
  "program": "CBACT01C",
  "caseId": "case20",
  "description": "Stored order is not read order. The three inline records are declared in DESCENDING key order, and app/cbl/CBACT01C.cbl:L29-L33 declares ACCTFILE as ORGANIZATION INDEXED with ACCESS MODE SEQUENTIAL over RECORD KEY FD-ACCT-ID, so the browse returns them in ASCENDING key order regardless of the order they were stored in. The expected line sequence is therefore the reverse of the seeded order, and the final state is stated in key order too. A translation that returned rows in insertion order would pass every other case in this set and fail this one.",
